# Testing Rules

## Contracts (Solidity)
- Use Foundry's built-in test framework (`forge test`)
- Comprehensive test coverage for all public/external functions
- Fuzz tests for math-heavy functions
- Fork tests for integration testing against live chains
- See `solidity.mdc` for naming conventions

## API (Hono)
- Test route handlers with Hono's built-in test client (`app.request()`)
- Test database queries against a Neon branch (not production)
- Mock external services (BounceTech API, etc.)
- Cover all error paths and edge cases

## Frontend (React)
- Unit tests only for core logic functions (formatting, calculations)
- Use Vitest if tests are needed
- No component tests unless specifically requested
- Focus test effort on contract and API layers
